<figcaption><strong>Fig P05.2.</strong> The powers of 3 walk the seven residue teams mod 7 in a fixed cycle of length 6: \(3 \to 2 \to 6 \to 4 \to 5 \to 1\), back to 3 (team 0 is never visited). Since \(77 = 6 \cdot 12 + 5\), the 77th step lands where the 5th step lands — on team 5 (red): \(3^{77} \equiv 3^5 \equiv 5 \pmod{7}\), so \(2026^{77} - 2026\) leaves leftover \(5 - 3 = 2\). Node positions and every arrow machine-verified in this pass's lab.</figcaption>
</figure>
